  {
    "id": "axie-gallery",
    "title": "Axie Gallery",
    "category": "digital",
    "categoryLabel": "Digital space",
    "subtitle": "A gallery beyond the physical",
    "description": "The Axie Gallery was born during COVID. Everyone was in isolation. Sick or not, everyone was struggling inside. The world seemed to stand still, and no one knew what would come next. Everyone needed to be healed.\n\nYiran imagined a building that is alive. It is a monster that lives alone deep in the forest, and it has the power to heal. It stands on a single leg. Its body rests on the treetops, held up by the branches, as if it were floating. The body is an undulating disc, a minimal surface, a bit like a Möbius strip, but with two sides. The two sides are life and death, yin and yang, two faces of the same body.\n\nEach side holds a room. On the bright side is the day room. Inside hangs a giant scroll of paper, and you write, and write, and write. When you finish the scroll, the window in the roof slowly opens, light pours in, and you are ready to return to the human world. On the dark side, beneath the body, is the night room. It is a room for sleep, filled with a magical liquid. As you fall asleep, the liquid washes away all your thoughts, and you recharge through the night.",
    "coverIndex": 4,
